"englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"28bbd2ac7d03c053b6db7510f4edf8a8d11e23324bd5a1e538e61a5dd6bca0c4","compact":"ccb5a1435aed16c9434c53435d6a28c461e62bfdf0ca19e8b302c7e151ccc779","nasal":"ccb5a1435aed16c9434c53435d6a28c461e62bfdf0ca19e8b302c7e151ccc779"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-47-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":47,"verse":10,"english":"Without making any distinction, do you, in my name, with folded hands, bow to my mothers-in-law and then ask the well-being of the kingdom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.754,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-48-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7047010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d5b5348e07445d35a0048904a4e85f40e0fafdb0d743d5b9fe8d2fffb1ac9b3b","compact":"5632aa2c6e4b2c0836846ca8d966dfe27ad4cd819b1f4815708e71213f303696","nasal":"c905ba2058b971b214f8e194e0a8fa9aa653650a6c0fe95f8408decdd04574c3"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-47-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":47,"verse":11,"english":"Do you tell further-more that king established in righteousness to treat the citizens as his brothers, to acquire piety by protecting his subjects duly for this is the greatest mortality and by this may be acquired excellent fame,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.692,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-48-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7047011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0f9fd55d5493760de73475e211457c2f4c13293bbf1037411d24c4c92d739c28","compact":"61bae4f1a44326c534eb0773b005ca04b772941f3ed4297ca53af9b91904dc28","nasal":"61bae4f1a44326c534eb0773b005ca04b772941f3ed4297ca53af9b91904dc28"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-47-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":47,"verse":12,"english":"Tell him that I am not sorry for my person-my greatest sorrow is that the citizens have vilified me.","alignmen